    {
      "block_id": "b00027",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The Prepare a Brief document provides a template that you can populate to issue to tenderers alongside the Invitation to Quote (ITQ) letter. It includes guidance on how to do this that can be deleted when the ITQ is ready for issue.",
      "ordinal": 27,
      "heading_path": [
        "Your Brief"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00028",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "To prepare a brief, you should gather information to help you make decisions on what your requirements are. This will include research on:",
      "ordinal": 28,
      "heading_path": [
        "Your Brief"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00029",
      "block_type": "table",
      "text": "Suppliers\tDo you have a current incumbent supplier? What is working in this contract/what is not? Are there suppliers available to quote for the work e.g. locally, regionally, nationally?\nKnowledgeable People/Experts\tTalk to people in the organisation who deal with the current contract – what do they want from a new contract? Talk with other buyers who have worked on a similar project. Talk with suppliers as part of early market engagement.\nMarket information\tHave there been any changes in the market? Are there any new innovations/technology?",
      "ordinal": 29,
      "heading_path": [
        "Your Brief"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {
        "rows": [
          [
            "Suppliers",
